# This mod ships no assembly and has nothing to build. The entry that earns its place here is
# .claude/: a session worktree is a full copy of the monorepo this folder came out of, hundreds
# of megabytes, and a session creates it in whatever folder it is working in.
#
# Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
# directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published folder
# is published. That is what Mod/ is for: the junction points there, and everything else in this
# folder - Art/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by construction.

# Claude Code session worktrees and their local settings.
.claude/

# Showcase working note: PROMPT_ACERTAINSERIES.md, French, holding the Preview and ModIcon
# prompts until both images exist. It lives at the monorepo root with every other mod's, which is
# where they are written and where PUBLISHING.md expects them. This rule is a guard only, in case
# a copy is ever made here: it is working notes in French, and this repository is public.
PROMPT_*.md

# DDS textures: not tracked. RimWorld writes one beside each PNG the first time it loads a mod
# (141 of them, 3.8 MB, on 2026-09-23). The PNG is the source and is what git holds; the game
# regenerates the rest. They stay on disk, and the publishing CI works from a git checkout, so
# it never ships them.
*.dds

# Pickle evidence stays on disk, never in git: captures and Player.log grow without limit.
# The durable record is one text line per run in docs/runs/ (see TESTING.md, "Evidence to keep").
Tests/Pickle/Evidence/
evidence/
